# Per-package statement-coverage floor, in percent.
#
# This file is the ratchet: CI fails when a package drops below its recorded
# floor, so coverage can only go up.
#
# The numbers are MEASURED, not aspirational. Each value below was taken on the
# v2 G1 tree with the command CI runs
#
#   go test -race -covermode=atomic -coverprofile=coverage.txt ./...
#
# then rounded DOWN by two to three points. The margin absorbs the only
# legitimate source of drift -- a test whose path depends on timing under
# -race -- and nothing else: a real regression is tens of points, not two.
# Measured at the time of writing: amr 100.0, authtest 87.6, webauthn 94.6.
#
# examples/passkeys is a runnable demonstration with no tests; it is listed at
# 0 on purpose so the gate does not treat it as an ungated package. `store`
# declares interfaces and sentinels only, has no statements, and so produces no
# coverage rows: the gate has nothing to measure and listing it would fail.
#
# Raising a floor after new tests land is a one-line change here. LOWERING one
# is a decision to accept a regression, and belongs in a review, not in a commit
# that was about something else.
#
# Every package with statements in `go list ./...` must appear. The gate refuses
# a package it has no floor for rather than passing it silently.
#
# Format: <package path relative to the module root> <floor percent>
amr 97
authtest 85
webauthn 92
examples/passkeys 0
